SC["a5c32_coda"]={img:"dawn",
 t:()=>SYS(`CODA — ONE MORNING, AFTER`)+((G.f.a5_door=="home")?(P(`The rain quit sometime before sunrise, without ceremony, as rain does.`)+P(`You wake in a bed exactly as small as you left it, under a ceiling you could map blind, in a house that smells like toast and someone burning toast, and for one long minute you lie still and listen to a world held up by nothing but physics: no chord, no warp, no watch-bell. Downstairs, a kettle. A radio talking about weather it cannot influence. Footsteps that you'd know in any heaven stopping outside your door, then deciding, with a little sister's whole imperious mercy, to let you sleep, and thundering down again.`)+P(`You get up anyway. There's a kitchen down there, and you know about kitchens now: they're the basement of every world, the room where the real ledgers are kept. You have forty years of breakfasts to attend and a hundred mornings of evidence to give to the one creditor who kept your light on. Some of it she'll believe. The toast gets made. The morning holds — on nothing, on habit, on love — and you stand at the window with your tea and watch an ordinary sky do its ordinary work, and of all the wonders in two heavens, you have decided this one is your favorite: it doesn't need you. It never did. It just wanted you home.`)):(""))+((G.f.a5_door=="open")?(P(`Dawn over the lake city comes up through ten thousand threads, and the light, as always now, arrives in CHORDS.`)+P(`You take tea on a gallery rail while the watch changes below: night-shift handing the sky to morning-shift, yawning, trading the small jokes of people who hold up heaven before breakfast. Out past the crossing-frame, the harbor's lamps go pale one by one. Somewhere down there a soul from an unimaginable weave is having its first morning: porridge, a blanket, a teacher with infinite patience pointing at the sun and saying the word for it. The arrivals' bell rang twice this week. Both met. Both named.`)+P(`It is, you think, watching the rota turn, the strangest thing you ever built: a world with a front door. Wide open, lamp lit, somebody always home. You finish the tea. The morning needs nothing from you for at least an hour, and you have learned — slowly, with professional help from every person who ever fed you — to let mornings be mornings. The sky holds. The door stands open. The kettle, somewhere, is already on.`)):(""))+((G.f.a5_door=="shut")?(P(`The first morning of the world's own sky comes up clean and unremarkable, which was the entire point, and you stand on the high gallery and watch it not need anyone.`)+P(`No arrivals' bell — never again. No thin places straining — the seam-watch's night report is one character long: HOLDS. The lake takes the light the way paper takes ink, the city wakes into its new arithmetic, and somewhere below a cook who holds a rota-shift on her rest days is shouting at a fish-seller in the voice of a woman who once held up one four-hundredth of heaven before lunch and expects a DISCOUNT.`)+P(`You carry the closed door like everything else permanent: noticed daily, regretted rarely, set down never. The sky you sewed shut is the same sky everyone else just calls weather. That's the victory. It will never once look like one, and it will hold for ten thousand mornings exactly like this, and you have come, over many teas, on many railings, to find that funnier than it is sad. Mostly. The kettle, somewhere, is already on.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The people the ledger kept. One last look around the table.`,go:"a5c32_table"}]};

SC["a5c32_table"]={t:()=>((G.f.a5_door=="home")?(P(`You keep them the way Sho kept a courtyard: inside, intact, load-bearing. Mei's wrist-thread, gone fine as a scar. Bao's laugh, surfacing in yours at inappropriate moments. A bookkeeper's bow; a blind woman's broom-rhythm in the rain on the glass; an old silk voice saying <i>stitch</i> as if it were a given name. Some mornings, at the window, your tea steams in eight bars or a kata's count or a solving sequence, and a sister watches you watch the sky, and asks nothing, and leaves the light on anyway, on principle. Two worlds. One boy. All threads accounted for.`)):(P(`They assemble as they always have: around food, without being summoned.`)+((G.mei>=3)?(P(`Mei, dispensing tea and triage in the same motion, having declared the morning a clinic on no authority but her own, which is the only authority she has ever needed.`)):(""))+((G.bao>=3)?(P(`Bao, narrating the porridge like a battle, fatter and happier and load-bearing in four supply chains.`)):(""))+((G.sho>=3)?(P(`Granny Sho and Suyin, shoulder to shoulder, bickering about sixty-year-old laundry with the deep contentment of women who have outlived a theology.`)):(""))+((G.f.ruan>=2)?(P(`Ruan, ledger at his elbow even at breakfast, entering the morning's blessings in the assets column, where — he will tell anyone who asks — they have always belonged.`)):(""))+((G.yan>=3)?(P(`Yan, off-duty and constitutionally unable to look it, practicing being warm with the same precision he gives a sword-form, and improving yearly.`)):(""))+((G.tang>=2)?(P(`And a letter from a mountain kitchen, cleaver-stroke characters, mostly soup advice, signed the way the basement signs everything it loves: MIND YOURSELF, DEAR.`)):(""))+P(`The morning holds. The table holds. You did not build either one alone, which is, in the end, the entire finding of the audit.`))),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`It is finished. The thread, the debt, the sky: all of it, at last, well tied.`,go:"end_final"}]};

SC.end_final={img:"title",t:()=>{
 const L=G.f.a5_loom||"woven",D=G.f.a5_door||"home";
 const T={woven_home:"THE MENDED SKY, AND THE LONG WAY HOME",woven_open:"THE HARBOR OF HEAVEN",woven_shut:"THE LAST FOREIGNER",
  free_home:"OWED NOTHING, GONE HOME",free_open:"THE KNOTLESS ROAD",free_shut:"ONE SKY, SEWN",
  heir_home:"THE STITCH THAT STAYS, THE STITCH THAT GOES",heir_open:"THE HEART THAT KNOCKS",heir_shut:"THE HEART OF HEAVEN"}[L+"_"+D];
 return '<div class="ending"><h3>ENDING: '+T+'</h3>'+
 P("<b>"+G.name+"</b>, who died at a bus stop in the rain and was sewn into a torn sky \u2014 servant of the kitchens, victor of the brackets, auditor of furnaces, the Knotless, Pattern Sage, "+(L==="heir"?"heart of heaven":L==="free"?"unmaker of the Grand Loom":"weaver of the counter-pattern")+".")+
 P("The Loom remembers its stitches. Every one. That was always the point.")+
 '<p class="small">Realm: <b>'+REALMS[G.realm]+'</b> \u00B7 Insight '+G.insight+' \u00B7 Body '+G.body+' / Mind '+G.mind+' / Heart '+G.heart+
 '<br>Threads in the anchor-ring: '+(G.f.a5_threads||1)+' \u00B7 The Golden Thread \u2014 complete, Acts I\u2013V</p></div>'+
 SYS("Thank you for playing. Nine endings wait across the matrix of loom and door \u2014 and the whole river is different at different insight, different friendships, different routes.");},
 c:()=>[{id:"t",l:"Return to the title screen (your finished thread is kept)",go:"start"},
  {id:"n",l:"\u2042 Begin a new thread (erases this save)",go:"start",do:()=>{localStorage.removeItem("gthread");G=fresh();}}]};
